<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19564" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gibbus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύπτω, κυφός</span>, bent, bowed,
			crooked; v. gibber, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>hunched</i>, <i>humped</i>, <i>gibbous.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calvaria ex interiore parte concava,
					extrinsecus gibba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 8,
					1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gibbus</span></b> , i,
				m., <i>a hunch</i>, <i>hump</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 10, 294</span></i>; <i><span class="en">309</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 109</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gibba</span></b> , ae,
				f., the same, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Dom. 23</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a hump-like
				swelling</i>, <i>protuberance</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
